Gate P1 cannot pass while P1-01 through P1-03 are open. The failures directly defeat the gate's identity, validated-document, and old-target atomicity claims even though every checked-in test passes. Remediation should be followed by a fresh independent review; the current reviewer should not self-certify those fixes.

R24 is a separate release/distribution blocker. It does not by itself prevent internal P1 engineering readiness, but it must remain BLOCKED and must not be reported as PASS.

